# Constrain the runtime deps to the exact versions the prod lockfile
# (and the Docker image) already pin, so the dev/test environment matches
# what ships. Without this, ``-r requirements.in``'s loose ``>=`` bounds
# re-resolve to whatever is newest at compile time, which is how
# requirements-dev.txt drifted from — and fell behind — requirements.txt
# (it predated the sentence-transformers/embeddings stack entirely, so
# ``make test`` failed on ModuleNotFoundError: numpy).
-c requirements.txt
-r requirements.in

# Testing
pytest
pytest-asyncio

# Linting
ruff
